A||N||35||TwisT||TwisT says his final Fiero-farewell....||||7||
Z||000000||TwisT||03-31-2001||01:29 AM||||My fellow Fiero lovers...<P>First,  sorry for being so vaccant on my last thread regarding the computer-enhanced Fieros...  I've been very busy the last few days...  <P>A while back I posted a topic in this forum about the fact that I might have give up my favorite hobby (Fieros!) because I was going to the Carribean to live.  Yes,  the CARRIBEAN!  <P>Well,  long story short...  time has come,  decisions are made...  and it's official;  I'm Carribean bound!  No specific date is set just yet,  but will more than likely be this fall before winter sets in.<P>What's this mean?  My '88 GT has to go...  I still have a lot of work to do to it before I can sell it though...  needs reassembly and paint,  along with a few other things.  I'm not going to enjoy this,  as many of you know I've had some big plans for it.  But I have to get rid of all of my debts,  and pretty much all of my posessions...  which includes my Fiero.  =(<P>Anyone need some furniature???  LOL...<P>Not much else to say.  I wanted to thank all of you on the forum for being so cool,  and for all the humor,  help and insight that everyone has provided me.  I've spent many late nights and early mornings participating in this forum and it is sad to leave it.<P>Trust me,  if I could take my Fiero with me,  I WOULD!!!<P>St. Martin is a small island though,  not much use for ANY car,  let alone a Fiero...  I'd be stuck driving in circles!  <P>Farewell...  and as a final thought,  a quote from Mel Gibson in the movie,  "Braveheart:"<P>"Every man dies,  not every man really lives..."<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carribean1.jpg">   <P>See you on the beaches of life!  *sniff-sniff*<P>Brett C. Aker<BR>Yankton,  South Dakota<BR>A.K.A. "TwisT"<BR>'88 Pontiac Fiero GT<BR>"ITALFIERO"<P>P.S.  Please send all plane-ticket contributions to:<P>Brett Aker<BR>604 Deer Blvd.<BR>Yankton,  SD 57078<P>Thanks!  LOL...  <P><p>[This message has been edited by TwisT (edited 03-31-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000001||sqoach||03-31-2001||01:56 AM||||aw man. sorry to see you go. you're a cool guy. funny guy too. so are you gonna sell me your fiero real cheap?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>j/k. later man. you'll be missed.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.JPG">  <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||9
Z||000002||Cheever2||03-31-2001||02:02 AM||||Wow, that was a shock.<BR>You'll be back... you're gonna be so miserable there: all that sun, those howling ocean breezes, the sunsets... it'll take it's toll (yeah, right).<BR>Well, drop in and see us!  Have fun!<BR>||||reg||9
Z||000003||GT Bastard||03-31-2001||09:07 AM||||That sucks a$$, dude.  But I hope you make a happy life there.  Best of luck to you.<P>-Bastard||||reg||1
Z||000004||Taijiguy||03-31-2001||09:29 AM||||I can't help but ask what you'll be doing there. What's the price for living in paradise?<BR>Best of luck-<BR>~Taiji||||reg||1
